clk: qcom: camcc-sm8450: park the RCGs on XO when disabled (shared RCG ops)

On the Galaxy Tab S8+ (SM8450) the first camera stream through CAMSS works
and every later one fails: the camera GDSC that collapsed after the session
(TITAN_TOP, or IFE_0 if TITAN_TOP was held up) never reaches power-up
complete ("status stuck at 'off'", GDSCR 0x68282800, CFG_GDSCR 0x010e0000).
A domain that collapsed after CCI traffic alone recovers.

Bisecting the VFE power cycle at runtime isolated vfe_set_clock_rates():
with the rate setting skipped in a throwaway power cycle, the following
stream works. The camcc register dumps show why. camcc-sm8450 registers
all 35 RCGs with clk_rcg2_ops, so when their branches are disabled the RCGs
keep their last configuration: ife_0_clk_src, csid_clk_src, cphy_rx_clk_src
and camnoc_axi_clk_src stay selected onto PLL0 and PLL3 outputs after the
PLLs have been powered down. The GDSC power-up sequence then waits on
domain clocks that never toggle. camcc-sm8550 and camcc-sm8650 use
clk_rcg2_shared_ops for every RCG, which parks the RCG on the XO source
(SRC_SEL 0 in every parent map here) while disabled and restores the
configuration on enable; downstream's 5.10 clock framework parks as well.

Switch every RCG in camcc-sm8450 to clk_rcg2_shared_ops.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
index d7c99e4b5..ff33c6978 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-sm8450.c
